Falsifies `machine_statistics_contract::verification::every_reading_is_total_over_an_admitted_page`.

The defect: the byte totals use a plain multiply where they must saturate, so a page whose frame
count and frame size multiply past `u64::MAX` panics the reader that admitted it (and wraps in a
release build). Real pages carry small numbers, so no host test with honest values reaches it.

Expected to fail: the multiplication overflow check in `total_bytes`, on any admitted page whose
total frames and frame size overflow when multiplied.

diff --git a/crates/machine_statistics_contract/src/lib.rs b/crates/machine_statistics_contract/src/lib.rs
index d70573b6e..bd91aa769 100644
